<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Naqsh-e Jahan Square</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Naqsh-e Jahan Square is a large public square in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, laid out under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> when he made the city the Safavid capital. It is framed by major monuments including royal mosques and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-qapu">Ali Qapu</a> palace. It stands as one of the most celebrated architectural achievements of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/naqsh-e-jahan-square.jpg" alt="Naqsh-e Jahan Square" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: احمد جمالی مقدم · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naqsh-i_Jahan_Square,_Jan._2018.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
